Title: Raid Phase 6 cannot obtain a gaze verdict from a background agent
Created: 2026-09-29
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-29T15:50Z claude created

--- body ---

## Context

Raid 0984/0987 (2026-09-29) launched Phase 6 exactly as `skills/raid/SKILL.md`
§ Phase 6 prescribes, one `/gaze` per PR as a background agent, and got no
review verdict from either run:

- **PR #1061** (8 files): the battery could not run. The isolation guard blocked
  git and writes aimed at the review worktree (ticket 0853's defect), and the
  `/review-pr` panel had no Agent tool, so no perspective ran
  (`PANEL-INTEGRITY: DEGRADED`, `dissent: unavailable`). Simplify and the gate
  did not run. Verdict ESCALATE.
- **PR #1060** (16 files): `/gaze` stopped at its 15-file size breaker
  (`skills/gaze/SKILL.md`, `circuit_breaker: un-reviewable`) before reviewing
  anything. Nothing in raid Phases 3-4 had compared the planned PR's file count
  with that breaker, although an ordinary ticket with its docs and tests reached
  16 files.

Both PRs merged on author decisions, backed by three `/review-pr` rounds from
`/hunt`, and for #1060 a targeted review of the unreviewed range. The raid's own
Phase 6 contributed nothing but two escalations.

Two defects, one contract:
1. **Nesting.** A raid is itself an agent orchestration; `/gaze` launched one
   level down cannot spawn its panel. Whether that is the Agent tool's absence in
   the child, the spawn-depth limit, or 0853's cwd pin, the raid prescribes a
   launch shape the harness cannot honour.
2. **Size.** The breaker is checked only at the last gate. Phases 3-4 should see it
   while splitting is still cheap.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A raid's Phase 6 yields a real `/gaze` verdict (panel ran, gate ran) for a PR under the size breaker, demonstrated on a fixture PR; or the raid skill states the launch shape that does (for example `/gaze` run by the orchestrator itself, or a headless `claude -p "/gaze N"` session), with the reason
- [ ] Raid Phase 4 (or Phase 3) flags a planned PR whose file count reaches the `/gaze` breaker, and proposes the split before execution
- [ ] A `/gaze` that cannot run its battery says so in one line naming the cause (guard, missing Agent tool, depth), distinct from a review finding
- [ ] `make check` passes
